msgid "You can also change telemetry settings using CLI:"
msgstr "你还可以使用 CLI 来更改遥测设置："

#: ../../source/features.rst:882
msgid ""
"How deep the traces go is a separate setting. By default PartCAD reports "
"the operations it names for itself -- the process a command is, and the "
"action each object it works on is -- and nothing below them:"
msgstr ""
"追踪深入到什么程度是一项单独的设置。默认情况下，PartCAD "
"只报告它为自己命名的那些操作——一条命令所对应的过程，以及它所处理的每个对象所对应的动作——再往下的内容一概不报告："

#: ../../source/features.rst:891
msgid ""
"``methods`` adds a span for every instrumented method underneath those, "
"which is what a trace needs to answer \"where inside this did the time "
"go\". It is expensive in a way that is easy to miss: creating one part "
"passes through a dozen instrumented methods, so a package of eight "
"thousand of them costs a quarter of a million spans to list. Turn it on "
"while you are looking at something, not for good."
msgstr ""
"``methods`` 会为这些操作下面每一个被插桩的方法都添加一个 "
"span，追踪要回答“时间究竟花在了它内部的哪里”正需要这些。它的开销大得很容易被忽视：创建一个零件要经过十来个被插桩的方法，因此光是列出一个有八千个零件的包就要付出二十五万个"
" span 的代价。只在你正查看某个问题时打开它，不要一直开着。"

#: ../../source/features.rst:898
msgid "``pc system telemetry info`` reports both settings."
msgstr "``pc system telemetry info`` 会报告这两项设置。"

#: ../../source/features.rst:901
msgid "Private Repositories"
msgstr "私有仓库"

#: ../../source/features.rst:903
msgid ""
"If you are systemically using PartCAD in your organization then it makes "
"sense to collect your own telemetry data to understand how the tool is "
"being used in your organization, and to learn how to improve your "
"organization performance."
msgstr "如果你在组织中系统性地使用 PartCAD，那么收集你自己的遥测数据是有意义的，这样可以了解该工具在你组织中的使用情况，并学习如何提升你组织的效能。"

#: ../../source/features.rst:907
msgid ""
"The only OpenTelemetry backend provider currently supported is `Sentry "
